    "group": [
      "pge:18823"
    ],
    "notes": "535-6 Sinan-ri, Jillye-myeon\r\nGimhae, Gyeongsangnam-do\r\n35.228361, 128.744247\r\n\r\nDedicated landing area you can see from take off once pointed out. \r\nTake off must be good as slope is gentle and trees border the area. \r\nIf taking off from alternate launch, you might have to bear left aroud the mountain edge and keep soaring to the left till you see the LZ.\r\nLZ is the 200m long area along the railroad. Area is quite confortable but rocks scattered in the grass make landing tricky, so need good restricted land field practice and adequate flaring. Be aware of Power lines. \r\nAlternate landing is easy accross the railroad if you can't make it to the official one.",
    "url": "https://www.paraglidingearth.com/?site=18823"
  },
